<file path="ansible/roles/k3s_cluster/K3S-BOOTSTRAP-README.md">
# K3s Cluster Bootstrap — README

This document covers the minimum steps required to provision, configure, and recover a 3-node HA K3s cluster using the Ansible playbook.

---

1. Prerequisites

VM Infrastructure
- Ensure k3s-pve2, k3s-pve3, and k3s-pve4 have been provisioned by Terraform.
- Verify target IPs in ansible/hosts/hosts.ini belong to VLAN20 (10.0.20.21–23).

Shared Cluster Token
Generate a 32-character hexadecimal token and save it into your encrypted vault:

openssl rand -hex 32
ansible-vault edit ansible/group_vars/all/vault.yml

Add to vault:
vault_k3s_cluster_token: "<your_generated_token>"

---

2. Bootstrapping a Fresh Cluster

Clean Up Prior Installs (If Retrying)
Run these commands on any node with a failed or partial installation before starting:

sudo /usr/local/bin/k3s-uninstall.sh
sudo rm -f /etc/rancher/k3s/cluster-initialized

Run the Playbook
Execute the deployment playbook from the root ansible/ directory using the symlink:

cd ansible/
ansible-playbook -i hosts/hosts.ini deploy_k3s.yml

Do not target playbooks/deploy_k3s.yml directly, or variables will not load.

---

3. Manual Steps After Deploying

Confirm Node States
kubectl get nodes -o wide

Verify Virtual IP VIP
curl -k https://10.0.20.20:6443/readyz
(A 401 Unauthorized response is the expected healthy signal.)

Register GitHub Deploy Key
sudo cat /etc/ansible-secrets/argocd_k3s_deploy.pub
Add the public key as a read-only Deploy Key in your repository settings.

Verify GitOps Sync
kubectl -n argocd get applications

---

4. Gotchas to Watch Out For

- Token Mismatches: All joining nodes must use the same token as the init node.
- Rejoin Logic Guard: The rejoin task uses a when: cluster_exists | default(false) guard to avoid failures when the VIP is not yet up.
- Playbook Targets: Ensure roles target hosts: k3s_cluster and are not attached to the localhost SSH-key play.
- NIC Configuration: kube-vip is hardcoded to eth0; update if your VM template or NIC naming differs.
- Local-Path StorageClass Warnings: A cosmetic error in journalctl -u k3s about Delete vs Retain is expected and safe to ignore.
- etcd-s3 Insecure Flag: For HTTP-only MinIO backends set etcd-s3-insecure: "true" rather than skipping validation.
- S3 Snapshot Syncs: Failed etcd backups do not retry continuously; they reconcile and sync the backlog on the next successful snapshot.
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/smartctl_exporter/defaults/main.yml">
---
smartctl_exporter_version: "0.14.0"
smartctl_exporter_arch: "linux-amd64"
smartctl_exporter_port: 9633
smartctl_exporter_user: smartctl_exp
smartctl_exporter_group: smartctl_exp
smartctl_exporter_bin_dir: /usr/local/bin
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/smartctl_exporter/handlers/main.yml">
---
- name: restart smartctl_exporter
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: smartctl_exporter
    state: restarted
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/smartctl_exporter/tasks/main.yml">
---
- name: Ensure smartmontools is installed (provides the smartctl binary itself)
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name: smartmontools
    state: present
    update_cache: true

- name: Create dedicated system group for smartctl_exporter
  ansible.builtin.group:
    name: "{{ smartctl_exporter_group }}"
    system: true
    state: present

- name: Create dedicated system user for smartctl_exporter
  ansible.builtin.user:
    name: "{{ smartctl_exporter_user }}"
    group: "{{ smartctl_exporter_group }}"
    groups: disk            # read access to /dev/sd*, /dev/nvme* device nodes
    system: true
    shell: /usr/sbin/nologin
    create_home: false

- name: Download smartctl_exporter release archive (checksum-verified against upstream sha256sums.txt)
  ansible.builtin.get_url:
    url: "https://github.com/prometheus-community/smartctl_exporter/releases/download/v{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}/smartctl_exporter-{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}.{{ smartctl_exporter_arch }}.tar.gz"
    dest: "/tmp/smartctl_exporter-{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}.tar.gz"
    # Ansible fetches this URL, finds the line matching the downloaded
    # filename, and verifies against it — no hardcoded hash to go stale
    # on a version bump. Same principle as the still-open SHA512 TODO on
    # the Debian VM image in infra-homelab; worth back-porting there too.
    checksum: "sha256:https://github.com/prometheus-community/smartctl_exporter/releases/download/v{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}/sha256sums.txt"
    mode: '0644'

- name: Extract smartctl_exporter archive
  ansible.builtin.unarchive:
    src: "/tmp/smartctl_exporter-{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}.tar.gz"
    dest: /tmp
    remote_src: true
    creates: "/tmp/smartctl_exporter-{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}.{{ smartctl_exporter_arch }}/smartctl_exporter"

- name: Install smartctl_exporter binary
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: "/tmp/smartctl_exporter-{{ smartctl_exporter_version }}.{{ smartctl_exporter_arch }}/smartctl_exporter"
    dest: "{{ smartctl_exporter_bin_dir }}/smartctl_exporter"
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0755'
    remote_src: true
  notify: restart smartctl_exporter

- name: Deploy smartctl_exporter systemd unit
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: smartctl_exporter.service.j2
    dest: /etc/systemd/system/smartctl_exporter.service
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0644'
  register: smartctl_exporter_unit

- name: Enable and start smartctl_exporter service
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: smartctl_exporter
    state: started
    enabled: true
    daemon_reload: "{{ smartctl_exporter_unit.changed }}"
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/smartctl_exporter/templates/smartctl_exporter.service.j2">
[Unit]
Description=SMART metrics exporter for Prometheus (smartctl_exporter)
Documentation=https://github.com/prometheus-community/smartctl_exporter
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User={{ smartctl_exporter_user }}
Group={{ smartctl_exporter_group }}
# smartctl needs raw ioctl access to query ATA/NVMe/SCSI devices. Rather
# than run the whole exporter as root (upstream's own docker-compose
# example does this), grant just the two capabilities smartctl actually
# needs. Ambient capabilities are inherited by the smartctl subprocess
# this binary shells out to (kernel >=4.3), so the child process doesn't
# need its own setuid/setcap — same restricted-service-account pattern
# as the minio user in nas_setup.
AmbientCapabilities=CAP_SYS_RAWIO CAP_SYS_ADMIN
CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_SYS_RAWIO CAP_SYS_ADMIN
NoNewPrivileges=true
ExecStart={{ smartctl_exporter_bin_dir }}/smartctl_exporter \
  --web.listen-address=:{{ smartctl_exporter_port }} \
  --smartctl.path=/usr/sbin/smartctl
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/wg_relay/handlers/main.yml">
---
- name: restart wireguard
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: "wg-quick@{{ wg_relay_interface }}"
    state: restarted
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/wg_relay/tasks/main.yml">
---
# iptables-persistent prompts interactively at install time ("save
# current IPv4 rules?") unless preseeded — without this, the apt task
# below can hang a Semaphore run indefinitely.
- name: Preseed iptables-persistent to skip the interactive save prompt
  ansible.builtin.debconf:
    name: iptables-persistent
    question: "{{ item }}"
    value: "false"
    vtype: boolean
  loop:
    - iptables-persistent/autosave_v4
    - iptables-persistent/autosave_v6

- name: Install WireGuard tools and firewall packages
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name:
      - wireguard-tools
      - iptables
      - iptables-persistent
    state: present
    update_cache: true

- name: Ensure WireGuard config directory exists, locked down
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: "{{ wg_relay_config_dir }}"
    state: directory
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0700'

- name: Generate WireGuard private key (idempotent — never overwrites an existing identity)
  ansible.builtin.shell: |
    set -o pipefail
    umask 077
    wg genkey > {{ wg_relay_private_key_path }}
  args:
    creates: "{{ wg_relay_private_key_path }}"
    executable: /bin/bash

- name: Lock down the private key file permissions
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: "{{ wg_relay_private_key_path }}"
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0600'

- name: Derive the public key from the private key
  ansible.builtin.shell: |
    set -o pipefail
    wg pubkey < {{ wg_relay_private_key_path }} > {{ wg_relay_public_key_path }}
  args:
    creates: "{{ wg_relay_public_key_path }}"
    executable: /bin/bash

- name: Read the generated public key back to the control node
  ansible.builtin.slurp:
    src: "{{ wg_relay_public_key_path }}"
  register: wg_relay_public_key_raw

- name: Show the relay's public key (needed for the OPNsense peer config)
  ansible.builtin.debug:
    msg: "Relay public key: {{ wg_relay_public_key_raw['content'] | b64decode | trim }}"

- name: Read the private key back for use in the interface template
  ansible.builtin.slurp:
    src: "{{ wg_relay_private_key_path }}"
  register: wg_relay_private_key_raw
  no_log: true

- name: Deploy wg0.conf
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: wg0.conf.j2
    dest: "{{ wg_relay_config_dir }}/{{ wg_relay_interface }}.conf"
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0600'
  no_log: true
  notify: restart wireguard

- name: Configure persistent IPv4 forwarding (needed to route between WireGuard peers)
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    dest: /etc/sysctl.d/99-wireguard-forwarding.conf
    content: |
      net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0644'
  register: wg_relay_sysctl_conf

- name: Apply sysctl changes immediately
  ansible.builtin.command: sysctl --system
  when: wg_relay_sysctl_conf.changed
  changed_when: true

# --- Host firewall ---
# Oracle's VCN Security List controls the network edge only. The
# instance's own iptables rules are a separate, independent layer that
# also defaults to blocking this — opening the Security List alone
# will NOT let WireGuard traffic through.
- name: Check whether the INPUT accept rule for WireGuard already exists
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -C INPUT -p udp --dport {{ wg_relay_port }} -j ACCEPT"
  register: wg_input_rule_check
  failed_when: false
  changed_when: false

- name: Allow the WireGuard UDP port through the host firewall
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -A INPUT -p udp --dport {{ wg_relay_port }} -j ACCEPT"
  when: wg_input_rule_check.rc != 0

- name: Check whether the FORWARD-in rule for wg0 already exists
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -C FORWARD -i {{ wg_relay_interface }} -j ACCEPT"
  register: wg_forward_in_check
  failed_when: false
  changed_when: false

- name: Allow forwarding in through the WireGuard interface
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -A FORWARD -i {{ wg_relay_interface }} -j ACCEPT"
  when: wg_forward_in_check.rc != 0

- name: Check whether the FORWARD-out rule for wg0 already exists
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -C FORWARD -o {{ wg_relay_interface }} -j ACCEPT"
  register: wg_forward_out_check
  failed_when: false
  changed_when: false

- name: Allow forwarding out through the WireGuard interface
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables -A FORWARD -o {{ wg_relay_interface }} -j ACCEPT"
  when: wg_forward_out_check.rc != 0

- name: Persist iptables rules across reboots
  ansible.builtin.command: "iptables-save"
  register: wg_iptables_save
  changed_when: false

- name: Write persisted rules file
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    content: "{{ wg_iptables_save.stdout }}\n"
    dest: /etc/iptables/rules.v4
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0644'

- name: Ensure wg-quick@{{ wg_relay_interface }} is enabled and started
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: "wg-quick@{{ wg_relay_interface }}"
    state: started
    enabled: true
</file>

<file path="ansible/roles/wg_relay/templates/wg0.conf.j2">
# Managed by Ansible — role: wg_relay. Do not edit by hand; changes
# will be overwritten on the next run.
[Interface]
Address = {{ wg_relay_address }}
ListenPort = {{ wg_relay_port }}
PrivateKey = {{ wg_relay_private_key_raw['content'] | b64decode | trim }}
{% for peer in wg_relay_peers %}

# {{ peer.name }}
[Peer]
PublicKey = {{ peer.public_key }}
AllowedIPs = {{ peer.allowed_ips }}
{% if peer.endpoint is defined %}
Endpoint = {{ peer.endpoint }}
{% endif %}
PersistentKeepalive = 25
{% endfor %}
</file>

